      "Unicred Ponto Capital is part of one of the main cooperative credit systems in the country. Founded in Santa Maria, in the state of Rio Grande do Sul, in 2013, marking the union of three cooperatives, it now has more than 7,000 members across 69 municipalities in the South and Northeast of Brazil. The concern to collaborate in building a more sustainable society has been evident since the organization's origins. The cooperative participates in its community beyond credit operations, thus identifying issues that are relevant to the local population. With this attentive outlook, Unicred Ponto Capital identified an ecological problem within the military units.\n\nThey were accumulating large volumes of uniforms, reporting a stock of up to 10 tons of textile waste. The lack of a structured solution led to the risk of disposal or incineration, which increases pollution and greenhouse gas emissions. At the same time, regions close to military units—such as the municipalities of Santa Maria, Santiago, Cachoeira do Sul, and Uruguaiana—faced high levels of social vulnerability, especially among female heads of household with low incomes, little education, and a lack of job opportunities. The circular economy is a possible response to combat both problems, stimulating productive inclusion and sustainable income generation. And that was precisely the path chosen by Unicred Ponto Capital to generate impact in its communities.",
